From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:18:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] PCI: apple: qualify the K116s for suspend-to-idle over
 the adopted N1 link

The adopted link's suspend check admits only the J716c; the K116s is its
OLED sibling with the same T6050 host and the N1 on port 0, and the
first s2idle attempt there failed with -EBUSY from the noirq suspend.
Let it through the same checks.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
[thomas: rebased onto integration, where the check also admits the K114c]
Signed-off-by: Thomas Glanzmann <thomas@glanzmann.de>

(cherry picked from commit aa16d423cf8a10e6bee0a79313a13fa9565292c6)
[k114s: from aurora-silicon/linux pull request 1647 (open), unchanged]
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
index dec95de35..64cf71162 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -5744,9 +5744,14 @@ static int apple_pcie_check_adopted_s2idle(struct apple_pcie *pcie)
 	struct apple_pcie_port *port;
 	int error = 0;
 
-	/* Other adopted platforms and deeper sleep remain unqualified. */
+	/*
+	 * Qualified on the J716c, the K114c and the K116s. The K116s is the
+	 * J716c's OLED sibling: the same T6050 host, the N1 on port 0. Other
+	 * adopted platforms and deeper sleep remain unqualified.
+	 */
 	if (!(of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j716c") ||
-	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k114c")) || !pm_suspend_no_platform())
+	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k114c") ||
+	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k116s")) || !pm_suspend_no_platform())
 		return -EBUSY;
 
 	if (!(readl(pcie->base + CORE_RC_CTL) & CORE_RC_CTL_RUN) ||
